Subject: [PATCH] Backport upstream page-backed FUSE readdir batching to 6.12.111

Based on upstream commits by Miklos Szeredi, Jaco Kroon and Matthew R. Ochs:
  467e245d47e6662a4cbf4184d9e6d0b1b120c0bf
  dabb90391028799fb524680feb4eb96eb904ca6f
  4dd6f6d3085a84e74b0a1efec3a05ed0b5125dce

Retain the userspace byte-count hint through VFS and OverlayFS. Bound FUSE
responses by negotiated max_pages, allocate order-0 pages, and use scatter-
gather output rather than a large virtiofs GFP_ATOMIC kvec bounce buffer.

Backport API changes only: alloc_pages_bulk_array; folio_descs/uses_folios;
combined folio-pointer/descriptor allocation instead of fuse_folios_alloc.
The unchanged parsers, directory cache and fuse_parse_result enum remain.
No tests were added by the three upstream commits. This backport is not yet
compiled or runtime-tested; guest-kernel correctness gates remain required.

